## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical end-to-end security for data integration pipelines, including artifact signing, attestation storage, and runtime enforcement with policy engines.

## Key Concepts

- Artifact signing with cosign and key management
- Attestations stored in Rekor registry
- Policy-driven runtime enforcement (Kyverno/OPA)
- Integration points with Kafka Connect

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal illustration: pseudo-check attestation reference in manifest
async function isAttested(manifest) {
  const ref = manifest.attestationRef;
  // fetch and verify against Rekor/public cosign key
  return !!ref;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle rotation of signing keys and revocation?
- What metrics and alerts would you add to detect failed attestations at startup?

## Why This Is Asked
Designing runtime access control is critical for microservices in a ride-hailing platform. This tests integration of SPIFFE identities, policy as code (OPA), and Envoy ext_authz in a real-world, zero-trust setup.

## Key Concepts
- SPIFFE IDs and mTLS identity
- Open Policy Agent (Rego) for authz decisions
- Envoy ext_authz as a gatekeeper
- Service mesh zero-trust patterns
- CI test harness for policy validation

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal JavaScript test harness exercising OPA policy via REST API
const fetch = require('node-fetch');
async function test(spiffe_id, expected) {
  const input = { spiffe_id };
  const res = await fetch('http://opa.local/v1/data/authz/allow', {
    method: 'POST',
    headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json' },
    body: JSON.stringify({ input })
  });
  const json = await res.json();
  console.log(spiffe_id, json.result === expected);
}
(async () => { await test('spiffe://domain.org/finance/payment', true); await test('spiffe://domain.org/unknown', false); })();
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical IR response for Vault/root token compromise in a multi-tenant Kubernetes setup with real-world sensitivity.

## Key Concepts
- Vault audit signals and root-token risk
- Token lifecycles, leases, re-sealing, key rotation
- Namespace scoping and RBAC in Vault
- Runbooks and alert thresholds

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example runbook trigger pseudo-code
if (vaultAudit.detects('root_login')) {
  revokeAllRootTokens();
  rotateRootToken();
  isolateNamespaces();
  rotateMasterKeys();
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test the runbook? 
- What metrics define a safe recovery window?
